  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A blown horn of laminated plate used at the Draining Ground to call the ninety minutes of dry sand at the lowest tides of the year. It gives two notes and nothing between them, the lower carrying about four kilometres downwind and the upper roughly half that. It was handed over in 2263 by a crier who had a better one, played once for the recording and not since. The mouth end is worn through the laminate into the second layer, which is a good ten years of use and possibly twenty.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
